      "Each family is recognized by its functional group: the functional group is the atom or set of atoms that gives a molecule its characteristic reactivity. Learn the table of functional groups by heart: it is the map of all organic chemistry.",
      "The most important organic reactions are addition (to a double or triple bond), substitution (one group leaves and another enters), elimination (a small molecule leaves and a double bond appears), condensation (two molecules join, losing water) and redox (oxidation and reduction of functions).",
