  "laboratorio": TranslatedTopic(
    title: "Chemistry laboratory",
    level: "Lab Practice",
    summary: [
      "The laboratory is where chemistry is touched with your hands: measuring, mixing, heating and observing. The first rule is safety: lab coat, goggles and gloves always; no eating or drinking; and know where the eyewash station, the shower and the fire extinguisher are before you start.",
      "Each piece of glassware has its use: the beaker and the Erlenmeyer flask are for mixing and heating, the graduated cylinder measures approximate volumes, the burette and the pipette measure precisely, and the volumetric flask prepares solutions of exact concentration.",
      "The basic techniques are filtration (separating a solid from a liquid), distillation (separating liquids by their boiling point), decantation (separating two immiscible liquids) and titration (finding a concentration with a solution of known concentration).",
      "Experimental error is measured: a measurement without its uncertainty says nothing. Always write down what you do, with units, and repeat measurements to check that they are reproducible.",
    ],
    formulas: [
      TranslatedFormula(name: "Density", expr: "d = m / V", note: "g/mL in the laboratory"),
      TranslatedFormula(name: "Absolute error", expr: "E = |measured value − true value|", note: "With units"),
      TranslatedFormula(name: "Relative error", expr: "%E = (E / true value) × 100", note: "Says whether the error is large or small"),
      TranslatedFormula(name: "Dilution", expr: "M₁V₁ = M₂V₂", note: "For preparing dilute solutions"),
      TranslatedFormula(name: "Molarity", expr: "M = n / V(L)", note: "The most used concentration in the laboratory"),
    ],
    exampleTitle: "Prepare 250 mL of 0.2 M NaCl (M = 58.5 g/mol).",
    exampleSteps: [
      "Moles needed: n = M × V = 0.2 mol/L × 0.250 L = 0.050 mol.",
      "Mass: m = 0.050 mol × 58.5 g/mol = 2.93 g of NaCl.",
      "Weigh 2.93 g on the balance and transfer it to the 250 mL volumetric flask.",
      "Add distilled water up to just below the mark, dissolve, and top up to the mark.",
      "Mix by stoppering and inverting the flask several times.",
    ],
    exampleAnswer: "Weigh 2.93 g of NaCl and make up to 250 mL in the volumetric flask.",
    errors: [
      "Reading the meniscus from the top: it is read at the bottom, with the eye at its height.",
      "Pouring water onto a concentrated acid: always the acid onto the water.",
      "Confusing the volumetric flask (exact volume) with the Erlenmeyer flask (approximate volume).",
      "Not writing down the data as you go: memory fails, the notebook does not.",
    ],
    tip: "Before weighing anything, write in the notebook what you are going to prepare, with the calculations already done. The laboratory is prepared on paper, not at the bench.",
  ),
  "color-iones": TranslatedTopic(
