      "The color in aqueous solution helps identify ions in a qualitative analysis, and the flame test is even faster: the flame excites the metal's electrons and when they return to their state they emit light of a characteristic color.",
      "Remember: the color depends on the ion, not on the whole compound. Cu²⁺ is blue both in the sulfate and in the nitrate, and Na⁺ colors the flame intense yellow whatever sodium salt it comes from.",
